  "slug": "unsupervised-highlight-reel",
  "title": "Unsupervised — Highlight Reel",
  "summary": "*Unsupervised* is part of *Machine Hallucinations*, Refik Anadol Studio’s ongoing exploration of data aesthetics. Since 2016, Anadol has utilized machine intelligence—specifically DCGAN, PGAN, and StyleGAN—as a collaborator to unfold unrecognized layers of reality. By processing vast digital archives, the studio creates multi-channel experiences that offer sensorial autonomy through cybernetic serendipity.\n\n*Unsupervised* processes 138,151 pieces of metadata from The Museum of Modern Art’s collection. Using StyleGAN2 ADA, Anadol trains a unique AI model to capture the machine’s transformative “hallucinations” of modern art in a 1024-dimensional space. By clustering image datasets into thematic categories, the work creates a latent cosmos where hallucinatory potential arises from interpreting over 200 years of art—from paintings to video games. This project echoes movements like Surrealism, which similarly explored automatism and chance to generate new forms.\n\nThe work pushes machine-learning research into new territories through Anadol’s dialogue with scholars like Jaakko Lehtinen of NVIDIA Research. Regarding the project, Lehtinen noted:\n\n<p class=\"m-l-56 display-inline-block\">This is the beauty of fundamental research: to see the progress we’ve made on a hard, technical machine learning problem being unexpectedly channeled to serve such astounding creativity is extremely satisfying. We’re thrilled to witness the deepening interplay between art and AI research, and eagerly looking forward to seeing what we can do together in the future.</p>\n\nThe resulting abstract images are dictated by the MoMA archive, with AI data pigmentation capturing movement within the latent space. Driven by edge-detection algorithms and colorized by latent coordinate density, the machine allows the artist to trace its “unconscious decisions” in a network of intricate, poetic connections.",
  "coverImage": "https://imagedelivery.net/iCRs13uicXIPOWrnuHbaKA/d8f78690-9464-492b-55ec-60806f971400/raw",
